{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be","id":572556,"title":"Changelings, how changed can you look/be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T06:04:49-07:00","id":572556,"title":"Changelings, how changed can you look/be?","content":"Hey everyone!<br /> In the old versions of Changeling I remember seeing art of changelings with horns, tails, hoofs, and kinds of stuff that would be hidden by the mask, and quite neatly so. Even people with antler horns can put on a cap without it getting stuck in their horns and so on and so forth. I loved it, I always loved how strange, mystic and even fairy-tale-like different characters would look. Once upon a time, I even had a &quot;the more out there, the better&quot;-point of view of what meins should look like.<br /> <br /> So here's my question, just where is the limit?<br /> Could I make a character who looks like a <a href=\"http://ak1.ostkcdn.com/images/products/8346144/8346144/Mermaid-Modern-Canvas-Print-Wall-Art-P15655860.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">mermaid</a>? Can I make a character with <a href=\"http://img4.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140821045938/disney/images/1/16/1561_Ursula_40_detail.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">tentacles</a> like Ursula from The Little Mermaid? Can I make a character with more limbs than you usually have, like <a href=\"http://orig09.deviantart.net/c180/f/2013/042/d/8/great_goddess_kali_by_khioora-d5udad3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Kali</a> of the hindu faith?<br /> <br /> Has this been talked about for the next version of changeling and if so, what are their conclusions?<br /> <br /> I'd think it'd be awesome to play a multi-limbed character, hell, make it a seeming for all I care!<br /> What do you guys think? Do or don't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:51:31-07:00","id":572633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be#post572556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahoy to ya!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has this been talked about for the next version of changeling and if so, what are their conclusions? </div> </div> </div>Miens far from human have been touched on, and, beyond a certain point, don't look to be in the cards. There was a section on the topic in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\">the Kiths sample preview</a> that the developer posted a couple of months ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kiths Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Limits of Transformation<br /> <br /> The Gentry can transform changelings into an almost infinite variety of forms, but even their reality-warping powers have some limits. Although they can take any possible form in Arcadia, when changelings enter the Hedge, return to the mortal world or even journey to a different realm controlled by another of the Gentry, they revert to a roughly humanoid form. The Gentry can permanently transform someone into a humanoid plant or even into a living statue made of solid ruby and they can make a changeling somewhat larger or smaller than normal, but they cannot permanently transform a human into a centipede or even a centaur. All transformations into radically non-human forms, are inherently unstable and if the changeling escapes from Arcadia or leaves the portion of Arcadia controlled by their Keeper, their natural humanoid form reasserts itself. <br /> <br /> Within their Keeper's realm, a changeling who appears as a human-shaped fire in the mortal world could have been a stationary pillar of flame, a wandering bonfire or even a single tongue of flame that was part of a vast fiery plain. The form that any changeling had in Arcadia may have been far less human than the form the changeling takes when they return to the mortal world.<br /> <br /> One reason that many changelings have so much difficulty remembering their experiences in Arcadia is that these experiences sometimes involved bodies or modes existence that are sufficiently alien that once the changeling is back in a mostly human form, they can no longer make sense of the memories they have of being a river or a living breeze. While some changelings were servants or warriors, others were sources for electrical energy, decorative fountains, portions of animate sandstorms or even living symphonies. Radically inhuman forms are common in many portions of Arcadia, but while a changeling's kith defines what sort of strange and utterly inhuman transformations they underwent, the extent of such transformations varies widely between changelings. One fireheart may have spent her entire time in Arcadia as a swift messenger whose form closely resembles her Mask, while another might have been a roaring fire in a his Keeper's great hall, or the night light her Keeper chatted with before sleeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:47:58-07:00","id":572731,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as I know, the Mien must be at least roughly humanoid, like said above. But you can have multiple limbs and still be roughly humanoid. I'd make multiple limbs into a Merit available to Wyrd 3+ changelings. The extra limbs don't let you attack more times per turn (combat is already pretty damn deadly in 2nd edition), but they might let you keep most of your Defense even against multiple opponents, for example. You could also say that it requires Willpower points to keep using extra limbs for long, if you think that's more balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:03:52-07:00","id":572765,"title":"","content":"Hmm, come to think of it, we haven't seen all of the Kiths that will be in the final game. While multiple arms does feel like the sort of thing better covered by a Merit,* I could see it potentially working as a Kith.<br /> <br /> * Unless a character has multiple limbs or unusual body structure with zero mechanical impact. I know I wouldn't much worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:33:35-07:00","id":572881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/572556-changelings-how-changed-can-you-look-be?p=572765#post572765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, come to think of it, we haven't seen all of the Kiths that will be in the final game. While multiple arms does feel like the sort of thing better covered by a Merit,* I could see it potentially working as a Kith.<br /> <br /> * Unless a character has multiple limbs or unusual body structure with zero mechanical impact. I know I wouldn't much worry about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple limbs kith? Multiple limbs merit?<br /> An action performed where a multiple limb is used (legs for athletics, arms for brawl, etc) can be re-rolled with a -1 penalty at spending x amount of glamor, and you must keep the second roll?<br /> <br /> And regarding the centaur comments and such, I can see how the mein would break the mask, coz well... You got a horse-arse. But an extra pair of arms could just be &quot;folded&quot; next to your other pair of arms. You'd look like you got thick arms, of course... And someone with mermaid fins instead of legs could just sit in a wheel-chair to avoid the mask breaking up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, as far as I know, the Mien must be at least roughly humanoid, like said above. But you can have multiple limbs and still be roughly humanoid. I'd make multiple limbs into a Merit available to Wyrd 3+ changelings. The extra limbs don't let you attack more times per turn (combat is already pretty damn deadly in 2nd edition), but they might let you keep most of your Defense even against multiple opponents, for example. You could also say that it requires Willpower points to keep using extra limbs for long, if you think that's more balanced. </div> </div> </div>This works too! Rerolls seem more logical to me from a thematic point of view though. &quot;Failed with these palms? Let's try the other ones!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}